    {
      "position": 8,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "Is there anyone that can break down this grammar more specifically for me? First off, I have never used this grammar before. To me, the 2nd example really seems like If Koizumi san is good in English, then he/she is also proficient in French. Having a conditional there really just makes no sense to me at all. If anyone could explain this better, it would be greatly appreciated !",
      "html": "Is there anyone that can break down this grammar more specifically for me? First off, I have never used this grammar before. To me, the 2nd example really seems like If Koizumi san is good in English, then he/she is also proficient in French. Having a conditional there really just makes no sense to me at all. If anyone could explain this better, it would be greatly appreciated !",
      "credits_raw": "NemosX",
      "content_sha256": "cb39f95c731bb27d79e12f10f4b48b01daed730aa346a0a7f62053ed79caa3c3",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 9,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "赤毛さん Thank you for replying to my post. I think I understand what your saying, by using the potential form of a the な adjective you get the same results as if you used a potential verb form, is that what you ment? いつも世話になってありがとうございます｡",
      "html": "赤毛さん Thank you for replying to my post. I think I understand what your saying, by using the potential form of a the な adjective you get the same results as if you used a potential verb form, is that what you ment? いつも世話になってありがとうございます｡",
      "credits_raw": "tigert",
      "content_sha256": "a4862233d029ce11424148638454fcdadc144499ecd900c06cf642cabba1f3d3",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 10,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "I intent to answer to Tigertさん. About the conditional form (条件形), we learned that this form apply to more words than verbs in japanese:\nVウ-Vエバ: する-すれば\nAイ-Aケレバ： 高い-高ければ\nAナ-Aナラ: 嫌[な]-嫌なら\nN-Nナラ: 雨-雨なら\nSomewhere も〜ば〜も and も〜なら〜も don't seem different.",
      "html": "I intent to answer to Tigertさん. About the conditional form (条件形), we learned that this form apply to more words than verbs in japanese:<br/>Vウ-Vエバ: する-すれば<br/>Aイ-Aケレバ： 高い-高ければ<br/>Aナ-Aナラ: 嫌[な]-嫌なら<br/>N-Nナラ: 雨-雨なら<br/>Somewhere も〜ば〜も and も〜なら〜も don't seem different.",
      "credits_raw": "赤毛",
      "content_sha256": "32daa11580499d0c7bf301413137fde39242a486a69f60501d0a597aa21ce7cf",
      "original_created_at": null,
